    {
      "id": "intro",
      "title": "开篇",
      "enter": "fade",
      "tone": "paper",
      "thumb": {
        "kicker": "开篇",
        "title": "开篇",
        "line": ""
      },
      "beats": [
        {
          "layout": "read",
          "reveal": "lines",
          "hold": 5318,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "你的思考能力，决定你人生的结果。",
              "pids": [
                "p1"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "这不是夸张。学会思考，从未像现在这样重要。",
              "pids": [
                "p2"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "尤其是自认为聪明的人，因为你最有可能像傻瓜一样思考。",
              "pids": [
                "p3"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "社交媒体上到处都是这样的例子。没有哪一天，你不会看到某个智商确实很高的人掉进显而易见的陷阱。",
              "pids": [
                "p4"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "pids": [
            "p1",
            "p2",
            "p3",
            "p4",
            "p1",
            "p2",
            "p3",
            "p4"
          ]
        },
        {
          "layout": "read",
          "reveal": "lines",
          "hold": 6020,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "有很多聪明人住在妈妈家的地下室里，再多吃一根薯条就要心脏病发作；也有很多笨人，却异乎寻常地快乐、健康、富有。",
              "pids": [
                "p5"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "我不打算谈第一性原理思维、系统思维、元认知，或者任何你能让 ChatGPT 教你的东西。我想给你一些不一样的东西。",
              "pids": [
                "p6"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "我们会从一维思维开始，慢慢推进到 5D 思维。",
              "pids": [
                "p7"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "如果你仔细读，就会体验到在一个新层次上思考是什么感觉。",
              "pids": [
                "p8"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "pids": [
            "p5",
            "p6",
            "p7",
            "p8",
            "p5",
            "p6",
            "p7",
            "p8"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "title": "你这么聪明，为什么还这么穷？",
      "enter": "fade",
      "tone": "paper",
      "thumb": {
        "kicker": "第 1 节",
        "title": "你这么聪明，为什么还这么穷？",
        "line": ""
      },
      "beats": [
        {
          "layout": "title",
          "reveal": "write",
          "hold": 5000,
          "title": "你这么聪明，为什么还这么穷？",
          "note": "本节标题取自已发布正文。",
          "en": "If you're so smart, why are you broke?"
        },
        {
          "layout": "quote",
          "reveal": "lines",
          "hold": 6000,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "quote",
              "text": "信念（faith）远胜于信条（belief）。信条是别人替你做了思考。",
              "attr": "——巴克敏斯特·富勒（Buckminster Fuller）"
            }
          ],
          "pids": [
            "p10"
          ]
        },
        {
          "layout": "read",
          "reveal": "lines",
          "hold": 5000,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "思考技巧第一条：",
              "pids": [
                "p11"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "如果你想理解某样东西是什么——比如天才级的思考——先弄清它不是什么，会很有帮助。",
              "pids": [
                "p12"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "这样，我们就能识别并避开愚蠢的思考。",
              "pids": [
                "p13"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "当我们观察愚蠢的思考是什么样子时，会得出几点洞见：",
              "pids": [
                "p14"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "pids": [
            "p11",
            "p12",
            "p13",
            "p14",
            "p11",
            "p12",
            "p13",
            "p14"
          ]
        },
        {
          "layout": "read",
          "reveal": "lines",
          "hold": 6500,
          "list": {
            "ordered": false,
            "start": 1,
            "items": [
              {
                "zh": "愚蠢的思考是一维的。人们试图把一切都塞进自己的视角，很难看到视角之外的东西。",
                "en": "Stupid thinking is one-dimensional. People try to jam everything into their own perspective and have difficulty seeing outside of it.",
                "pids": [
                  "p15"
                ]
              },
              {
                "zh": "愚蠢的思考是还原论的。比如，某个领域（例如商业）的专家，试图把一切都归结为一个\"策略\"问题。",
                "en": "Stupid thinking is reductionistic. Experts in one domain, like business, try to reduce everything to a \"strategy\" problem, as an example.",
                "pids": [
                  "p16"
                ]
              },
              {
                "zh": "愚蠢的思考是部落式的。你只信任你的群体、党派或部落，认为其他所有人都是错的，因为他们不顺从。",
                "en": "Stupid thinking is tribal. You only trust your group, party, or tribe and consider everyone else wrong because they don't conform.",
                "pids": [
                  "p17"
                ]
              },
              {
                "zh": "愚蠢的思考不提问。你的理由是\"事情就是这么做的\"。",
                "en": "Stupid thinking does not question. Your justification is \"that's just how it's done.\"",
                "pids": [
                  "p18"
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "pids": [
            "p15",
            "p16",
            "p17",
            "p18",
            "p15",
            "p16",
            "p17",
            "p18"
          ]
        },
        {
          "layout": "read",
          "reveal": "lines",
          "hold": 8432,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "总体而言，愚蠢的思考就是：一旦触及自己所知的边界，就把心智关上。",
              "pids": [
                "p19"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "愚蠢的思考，就是过早停止思考。到了某个点，你就用预先编好的念头做出反应，再也得不到任何新颖的洞见。",
              "pids": [
                "p20"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "据此，我们可以试着给天才思考下一个像样的定义。它可能是：",
              "pids": [
                "p21"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "它是一种能力：把带有威胁性的观念，也放进“可能性”的领域里容纳下来；再配上一种意图——你想要“理解”，而不只是“知道”。天才思考的标志，体现在你思考的宽度、深度和高度上。在这些维度上，你能不断向外探索，不会中途被截断——这种截断，往往是因为你把某个观念当成了绝对真理。它是你遍历那张完整、普遍的观念之网（现实、所有潜在的知识），并把它们整合成某种连贯或有用的东西的能力——哪怕那不是全新的东西。",
              "pids": [
                "p22"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "pids": [
            "p19",
            "p20",
            "p21",
            "p22",
            "p19",
            "p20",
            "p21",
            "p22"
          ]
        },
        {
          "layout": "read",
          "reveal": "lines",
          "hold": 9152,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "那么问题来了：“知道”和“理解”有什么区别？怎么培养思考的宽度、深度和高度？如果你还能走得更远呢？",
              "pids": [
                "p23"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "“知道”是横向的。你在某个特定领域学大量知识、记住大量事实，直到变得胜任。知道很多的人被称为“专家”，可当今世界并不需要更多专家。",
              "pids": [
                "p24"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "“理解”是纵向的。它关乎你整套认知操作系统有多精密。一个人可以知道得很少，却理解得很多，还能用这种洞见去行动，带来更有价值的结果。",
              "pids": [
                "p25"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "“聪明的笨人”现象，源于横向很先进、纵向却卡住了。一个坐拥全世界的钱、却发现自己不快乐的商人。一个作品很美、却没法靠它谋生的创意人。一个连一段稳定关系都维持不了的肌肉男。他们在各自的领域里知道很多，却看不到自己知识泡泡之外的东西。那个知识泡泡，没有提供足够的表面积，让他们识别并解决那些导致痛苦的问题。",
              "pids": [
                "p26"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "claim",
              "text": "这就是为什么学会如何思考如此重要。",
              "pids": [
                "p27"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "pids": [
            "p23",
            "p24",
            "p25",
            "p26",
            "p27",
            "p23",
            "p24",
            "p25",
            "p26",
            "p27"
          ]
        },
        {
          "layout": "read",
          "reveal": "lines",
          "hold": 5678,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "因为你的心智，就是你与现实互动的方式。",
              "pids": [
                "p28"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "你处理信息 → 理解它（思考）→ 做出选择 → 接收作为反馈的信息 → 回应反馈，并重复这个循环。",
              "pids": [
                "p29"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "那么，思考决定了你人生的结果。",
              "pids": [
                "p30"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "你每一刻的愚蠢思考，都会累积成一种复利效应，把你挖进一道深深的车辙里——深到你甚至够不着那个能把你带出来的念头。",
              "pids": [
                "p31"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "pids": [
            "p28",
            "p29",
            "p30",
            "p31",
            "p28",
            "p29",
            "p30",
            "p31"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "title": "思考的高度、层级和线",
      "enter": "fold",
      "tone": "dusk",
      "thumb": {
        "kicker": "第 2 节",
        "title": "思考的高度、层级和线",
        "line": ""
      },
      "beats": [
        {
          "layout": "title",
          "reveal": "write",
          "hold": 5000,
          "title": "思考的高度、层级和线",
          "titleSize": "quiet",
          "note": "本节标题取自已发布正文。",
          "en": "Altitudes, levels, and lines of thinking"
        },
        {
          "layout": "quote",
          "reveal": "lines",
          "hold": 6000,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "quote",
              "text": "你无法在制造问题的同一意识层次上解决问题。",
              "attr": "——阿尔伯特·爱因斯坦"
            }
          ],
          "pids": [
            "p33"
          ]
        },
        {
          "layout": "read",
          "reveal": "lines",
          "hold": 5372,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "我们从地基开始。",
              "pids": [
                "p34"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "思考的“线”（lines），是你可以知道很多的领域。",
              "pids": [
                "p35"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "线代表横向发展（宽度）。",
              "pids": [
                "p36"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "它们可以是任何东西：营销、天体物理、政治、社会动力学、宗教，等等。当你试图学习某个特定领域的知识，你就是在增加那条思考线的宽度。就像在电子游戏里攒经验值。",
              "pids": [
                "p37"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "pids": [
            "p34",
            "p35",
            "p36",
            "p37",
            "p34",
            "p35",
            "p36",
            "p37"
          ]
        },
        {
          "layout": "read",
          "reveal": "lines",
          "hold": 5000,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "（顺便说一句，如果你研究过肯·威尔伯（Ken Wilber），就能看出我在说什么——只是把它用在了思考上。）",
              "pids": [
                "p38"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "pids": [
            "p38",
            "p38"
          ]
        },
        {
          "layout": "figure",
          "reveal": "lines",
          "hold": 4500,
          "figure": {
            "src": "../img/07_1.jpg",
            "alt": "四层能力成长图：从新手到高手"
          }
        },
        {
          "layout": "read",
          "reveal": "lines",
          "hold": 5000,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "思考的“层级”（levels），是你如何思考每一条线。",
              "pids": [
                "p39"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "层级代表纵向发展（深度）。",
              "pids": [
                "p40"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "观察认知发展在集体和个体身上、随时间如何演化，我们会注意到 5 种核心模式：",
              "pids": [
                "p41"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "pids": [
            "p39",
            "p40",
            "p41",
            "p39",
            "p40",
            "p41"
          ]
        },
        {
          "layout": "read",
          "reveal": "lines",
          "hold": 7028,
          "list": {
            "ordered": false,
            "start": 1,
            "items": [
              {
                "zh": "本能型（第 0 级）——你生来出于纯粹的生存需要而行动。你对刺激做出反应，中间几乎没有思考。",
                "en": "Instinctual (Level 0) – You are born act out of the need for pure survival. You react to stimuli with little thinking in between.",
                "pids": [
                  "p42"
                ]
              },
              {
                "zh": "从众型（第 1 级）——非黑即白的思维。你遵守规则，服从权威，不加质疑。你采纳别人的视角。",
                "en": "Conformist (Level 1) – Black and white thinking. You follow rules and obey authority without questioning. You adopt others perspective.",
                "pids": [
                  "p43"
                ]
              },
              {
                "zh": "个人主义型（第 2 级）——批判性思维出现，你构建自己的模型。你建立自己的视角。",
                "en": "Individualist (Level 2) – Critical thinking emerges and you construct your own model. You build your own perspective.",
                "pids": [
                  "p44"
                ]
              },
              {
                "zh": "综合型（第 3 级）——你把自己的模型看作众多模型之一。你能容纳矛盾，把视角当作工具，而不是法律或某种不容置疑的真理。",
                "en": "Synthesist (Level 3) – You see your model as one among many. You hold contradictions and use perspectives as tools rather than law or some unquestionable truth.",
                "pids": [
                  "p45"
                ]
              },
              {
                "zh": "生成型（第 4 级）——你创造出以前不存在的原创视角，或者在没有外部影响的情况下得出观念。",
                "en": "Generative (Level 4) – You create original perspectives that didn't exist before, or you come to ideas without outside influence.",
                "pids": [
                  "p46"
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "pids": [
            "p42",
            "p43",
            "p44",
            "p45",
            "p46",
            "p42",
            "p43",
            "p44",
            "p45",
            "p46"
          ]
        },
        {
          "layout": "read",
          "reveal": "lines",
          "hold": 7100,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "第 1 级和第 2 级可以看作“第一层”（first tier）思维，过于教条。我对，你错。",
              "pids": [
                "p47"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "第 3 级和第 4 级可以看作“第二层”（second tier）思维，它们拒绝教条，寻求那处在中间的终极真理。",
              "pids": [
                "p48"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "在意义的领域里，你往往先被灌输一套信仰体系，然后质疑它、得出自己的结论（常常把先前那套推翻），接着开始在所有信仰体系里都看到真理，最后，你有能力创造一套更宽广的体系。",
              "pids": [
                "p49"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "在政治上，我们看到的许多争斗和暴力，都是因为大众还运作在第 1 级和第 2 级。我的群体对你的群体。双方都无法跳出自己的泡泡去思考。",
              "pids": [
                "p50"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "pids": [
            "p47",
            "p48",
            "p49",
            "p50",
            "p47",
            "p48",
            "p49",
            "p50"
          ]
        },
        {
          "layout": "read",
          "reveal": "lines",
          "hold": 8414,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "p",
              "text": "再说一遍，我要把这点说得极其清楚，因为这陷阱太容易掉进去了：",
              "pids": [
                "p51"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "p",
